Breaks: kidux-module-scratch (<< 15.2.0+build2.3~),
        kidux-module-turbowarp (<< 0+git20260915.3~),
Description: Kidux web applications, for learning modules made of web pages
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This package is
 what learning modules made of web pages need: a small server that serves
 them on this computer only, and Chromium, opened on one of them at a time
 in a window with no tabs and no address bar, and held to that server and
 nothing else, so a link out of a learning module leads nowhere. A module
 that opens a website on the internet names the site's hosts, and its
 Chromium reaches those and nothing more.
 .
 The managed policy is written from the installed modules whenever one is
 installed or removed, and applies to every use of Chromium on this
 computer.
